{"company":{"ticker":"CRM","name":"Salesforce","sector":"Technology","industry":"Software","size":"large","cik":1108524},"scores":{"growth":56.0,"quality":61.0,"value":84.0,"acceleration":39.0,"price_momentum":79.0,"reality":52.0,"pricing":44.0},"strategist":{"ticker":"CRM","opportunity_score":67.0,"components":{"structural_trend":72.0,"capital_flow":81.0,"acceleration":39.0,"quality":61.0,"valuation":84.0,"estimate_revisions":null,"management_commentary":null,"narrative_acceleration":null,"insider_institutional":null},"weights":{"structural_trend":0.2,"capital_flow":0.1,"acceleration":0.15,"quality":0.15,"valuation":0.15,"estimate_revisions":0.1,"management_commentary":0.05,"narrative_acceleration":0.05,"insider_institutional":0.05},"coverage":0.75,"unavailable":{"estimate_revisions":"Estimate-revision feed (Phase 2)","management_commentary":"Earnings Intelligence Engine (Phase 2)","narrative_acceleration":"Narrative Intelligence Engine (Phase 2)","insider_institutional":"Form 4 / 13F ingestion (Phase 2)"},"reality":59.0,"narrative":71.0,"pricing":47.0,"expectations_gap":13.0,"macro_fit":53.0,"sector_rotation":66.0,"theme_pricing":53.0,"checks":[{"label":"Revenue accelerating","ok":false,"evidence":"TTM growth +11.2% vs +11.0% prior quarter"},{"label":"FCF improving","ok":true,"evidence":"FCF growth +21.3%, FCF margin +34.5%"},{"label":"ROIC expanding","ok":false,"evidence":"ROIC +11.3%, incremental ROIC +4.9%"},{"label":"Margins expanding","ok":false,"evidence":"Operating margin +19.9% (-34 bps YoY)"},{"label":"Theme exposure strengthening","ok":true,"evidence":"Exposure-weighted theme trend 72.0"},{"label":"Capital rotating toward sector","ok":true,"evidence":"Technology rotation score +66"},{"label":"Valuation below own history","ok":true,"evidence":"Cheapness vs 5y history 89.0/100"},{"label":"Valuation below sector peers","ok":true,"evidence":"Sector-relative value score 84.0"},{"label":"Balance sheet strong","ok":false,"evidence":"Net debt/EBITDA 2.7"},{"label":"Not diluting shareholders","ok":true,"evidence":"Diluted share count -7.4% YoY"},{"label":"Analyst estimates moving higher","ok":null,"evidence":"Estimate-revision feed not connected (Phase 2)"},{"label":"Management guidance increasing","ok":null,"evidence":"Earnings Intelligence Engine not built (Phase 2)"}],"thesis":"Salesforce (CRM) screens at opportunity 67.0 with an expectations gap of 13.0. Reality 59.0 reflects +11.2% TTM revenue growth, +19.9% operating margin and +11.3% ROIC; pricing 47.0 reflects a fair multiple and strong price momentum. Primary theme exposure: AI Software & Agents (trend 72.0). Macro fit for Technology in a Goldilocks regime is 53.0/100.","market_expectation":{"summary":"Priced for stagnation or deterioration; the market is not paying for improvement.","evidence":["EV/Sales 5.1x (17.0th pct of own 5y range)","P/E 20x (0.0th pct of own history)","FCF yield 7.7%","PEG 0.3","12m return -3%, -10% from 52w high"]},"what_market_misses":["Reality (59.0) is running ahead of what is priced (47.0): an expectations gap of +13 pts.","Its main theme (AI Software & Agents) has trend 72.0 vs pricing 53.0: the theme itself is under-owned."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (roughly 90 days after the last filing on 2026-08-27)","AI Software & Agents: evidence that 'Trust, integration into workflows, proprietary data' is easing via Platforms owning the system of record and the data","Continued rotation into Technology"],"risks":["No engine-flagged risks; standard execution and macro risk apply."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 6% (currently 11.2%)","ROIC falls below 7% (currently 11.3%)","Operating margin compresses more than 200 bps YoY (currently 19.9%)","Technology rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive runs (currently +66)","Adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55%","Price closes >10% below its 200-day average with negative relative strength","AI Software & Agents theme trend drops below 45"],"break_rules":[{"id":"revenue_growth","label":"TTM revenue growth","metric":"revenue_growth","op":"<","threshold":0.0623,"current":0.1123},{"id":"roic","label":"ROIC","metric":"roic","op":"<","threshold":0.0727,"current":0.1127},{"id":"margin","label":"Operating margin change YoY","metric":"operating_margin_change","op":"<","threshold":-0.02,"current":-0.003389435487615805},{"id":"rotation","label":"Technology rotation score","metric":"sector_rotation","op":"<","threshold":-20,"consecutive":2,"current":66.0},{"id":"regime","label":"P(Stagflation)+P(Contraction)","metric":"adverse_regime_prob","op":">","threshold":55,"current":48.9},{"id":"trend","label":"Distance from 200dma","metric":"dist_200dma","op":"<","threshold":-10,"and_negative_rs":true,"current":18.3},{"id":"theme","label":"AI Software & Agents theme trend","metric":"theme_trend","theme_id":"ai-software-agents","op":"<","threshold":45,"current":72.0}],"narrative_note":"Narrative from the last 7 morning briefs' theme signals (exposure-weighted).","llm_enriched":true,"theme_exposures":[{"theme_id":"ai-software-agents","theme":"AI Software & Agents","weight":0.5,"order":1,"effective":0.5}],"llm":{"thesis":"Salesforce is priced at the very bottom of its own valuation history (P/E 20x = 0th percentile vs a 5y median of 87x; EV/Sales 5.1x = 17th percentile; 7.7% FCF yield) while still compounding revenue at +11.2% TTM with a 34.5% FCF margin and FCF growth of +21.3%. That gap \u2014 engine reality 59 vs pricing 47, a +13pt expectations gap \u2014 is the trade: the market has re-rated CRM as a structurally impaired seat-based SaaS incumbent facing agentic disruption, not as a cash machine retiring 7.4% of its shares a year. The honest bear case is visible in the numbers too: incremental ROIC of 4.9% sits below ROIC of 11.3% and almost certainly below cost of capital, operating margin slipped 34bps YoY, and net debt/EBITDA of 2.7x is unusually levered for a software franchise \u2014 capital allocation, not demand, is the defect. The asymmetry is that at 13x FCF you are paid to wait: even flat growth and no multiple expansion yields high-teens shareholder yield, while any evidence that AI agents monetize on top of the system of record rather than around it re-rates the multiple. Own it as a cash-return-plus-optionality position, sized for the fact that the de-rating reflects a real debate, not a mistake.","fundamental_read":"Growth is stable-not-accelerating (+11.2% TTM vs +11.0% prior) but cash conversion is exceptional: $15.15B FCF on $43.9B revenue, 34.5% FCF margin, 1.57x FCF/net income, only $596M capex. Profitability quality is mixed \u2014 77.3% gross margin and 25.2% ROE are strong, but 19.9% operating margin fell 34bps YoY, SBC is 8.3% of revenue, and incremental ROIC of 4.9% says recent capital (M&A and the debt behind it) is being deployed below the corporate return. The balance sheet is the weak link: $39.3B debt against $11.4B cash, net debt/EBITDA 2.7x, interest coverage 8.9x \u2014 serviceable but it constrains further large acquisitions and makes the aggressive buyback ($35.07B, share count -7.4%) a leveraged bet on its own equity.","technical_read":"Primary trend is intact and improving: price 18.3% above the 200-day, 50-day above the 200-day, and a violent +58.6% three-month move off a washed-out base even though the 12-month return is still -2.6% and the stock sits 10.5% below its 52-week high. Short term the move is digesting \u2014 close of 238 is below the 20-day (249), MACD histogram is negative at -4.14, and RSI 53 is neutral, which argues for entry on pullbacks toward the rising 50-day (~212) rather than chasing. Structure stays constructive unless price loses the 200-day (~201) on relative weakness.","market_expectation":"At 20x earnings, 5.1x EV/Sales and a 7.7% FCF yield against a 5-year median P/E of 87x, the market is underwriting terminal-value impairment: that agentic AI collapses seat-based pricing, that net revenue retention drifts toward low-single-digit growth, and that the $27.9B net debt was spent on assets earning ~5% incremental returns. In other words, consensus is paying for the cash flows in hand and assigning roughly zero option value to Agentforce/Data Cloud monetization or margin expansion. The 3-month +58.6% move suggests positioning has begun to shift, but the absolute multiple says the re-rating is early, not finished.","what_market_misses":["Valuation percentile is doing the work: P/E at the 0th percentile and P/FCF at the 10th percentile of a five-year range means the bar for a positive surprise is mechanically low \u2014 stable 11% growth plus an 18.7% shareholder yield produces equity returns without any multiple expansion.","The engine's reality score (59) leads pricing (47) by 13 points, and the primary theme (AI Software & Agents, trend 72) is itself priced at only 53 \u2014 CRM is an under-owned proxy for an under-owned theme.","Buybacks at 20x earnings are a genuinely accretive use of capital in a way they were not at 87x; the -7.4% diluted share count is quietly doing more for per-share value than any acquisition of the last cycle.","FCF is growing 21.3% \u2014 roughly double revenue growth \u2014 which means cash generation is improving even as reported operating margin ticked down 34bps; the market is anchoring on the margin headline, not the cash.","Sector rotation is +66 into Technology while every other sector except Energy is deeply negative; CRM is the cheapest large-cap way to express that rotation without paying an AI-premium multiple."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (~90 days after the 2026-08-27 filing): any print showing Agentforce/data-layer revenue disclosed separately, or cRPO reacceleration above 11%, directly attacks the terminal-decline narrative.","Continued buyback execution \u2014 sustaining a ~7% annual share count reduction at these multiples compounds EPS regardless of top-line.","Evidence that the theme's bottleneck ('trust, integration into workflows, proprietary data') is easing in favor of platforms that own the system of record, which is exactly CRM's structural claim.","Deleveraging: debt paydown taking net debt/EBITDA meaningfully below 2.7x would remove a real overhang and free capital allocation.","Persistent Technology rotation (+66) pulling generalist flows into the cheapest quality names in the sector."],"risks":["Incremental ROIC of 4.9% is the central red flag \u2014 if management responds to slowing organic growth with another large debt-funded acquisition, the thesis converts from cash-return story to value trap.","Agentic AI genuinely deflating per-seat SaaS pricing: 11.2% growth that is not accelerating gives no evidence yet that AI is additive rather than substitutive.","Operating margin already slipped 34bps YoY while SBC runs at 8.3% of revenue; AI infrastructure and model costs could compress margins further just as the market demands proof of margin expansion.","Leverage of 2.7x net debt/EBITDA limits flexibility if the macro regime shifts \u2014 Stagflation (23.5%) plus Contraction (25.4%) is ~49% of the probability mass versus 26.6% Goldilocks.","The stock has already run +58.6% in three months with a negative MACD; a crowded mean-reversion trade can give back a large share of that quickly.","Estimate-revision and management-guidance feeds are not connected, so the thesis rests on trailing fundamentals and valuation rather than forward signal \u2014 a material coverage gap (0.75)."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 6% (currently 11.2%), confirming seat-based erosion rather than digestion.","ROIC falls below 7% or incremental ROIC stays under ~5% for consecutive periods while leverage rises \u2014 i.e., another value-destructive acquisition.","Operating margin compresses more than 200bps YoY from 19.9%, indicating AI costs are structural rather than transitional.","FCF margin falls below ~28% or FCF growth turns negative, removing the cash-yield floor under the valuation.","Buyback pace slows materially (share count reduction under ~2% annualized) while leverage stays above 2.7x.","Price closes more than 10% below the 200-day (~201) with negative relative strength versus the sector.","Technology rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive runs, or AI Software & Agents theme trend drops below 45.","Combined Stagflation + Contraction regime probability exceeds 55%."],"second_order_beneficiaries":["Hyperscalers and inference compute providers: every agent Salesforce deploys runs on someone's silicon and someone's cloud, and CRM's low capex ($596M on $43.9B revenue) means it rents rather than builds that capacity.","Data integration, pipeline and ETL/reverse-ETL vendors: the stated theme bottleneck is 'integration into workflows, proprietary data' \u2014 the system of record is only valuable to agents once it is unified and queryable.","Vector/analytics database and data-warehouse platforms that sit underneath agent retrieval, where CRM's own data layer must interoperate rather than monopolize.","Global systems integrators and consultancies: agentic deployments are configuration- and change-management-heavy, and incumbent enterprise software rollouts historically spend multiples of license cost on services.","Identity, governance, observability and AI-evaluation vendors: 'trust' is explicitly the gating constraint for agent adoption in regulated enterprise workflows.","Credit markets and the investment banks intermediating them: with $39.3B debt and a $35B buyback program, CRM is a structurally large issuer and repurchase client regardless of operating outcome."],"epistemic_labels":[{"statement":"P/E is 20.3x, at the 0th percentile of its own 5-year range versus a median of 87x; EV/Sales 5.1x at the 17th percentile.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"TTM revenue growth is +11.2% versus +11.0% prior quarter; operating margin 19.9%, down 34bps YoY.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"FCF of $15.15B on $43.9B revenue (34.5% margin), FCF growth +21.3%, FCF yield 7.7%.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Diluted share count down 7.4% YoY with $35.07B of buybacks; shareholder yield 18.7%.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Net debt $27.9B, net debt/EBITDA 2.7x, interest coverage 8.9x.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"ROIC 11.3% but incremental ROIC only 4.9%.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Price is 18.3% above the 200-day and +58.6% over three months, but -2.6% over twelve months and 10.5% below the 52-week high; MACD histogram negative, RSI 53.","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"The market is underwriting terminal impairment of seat-based SaaS economics from agentic AI, hence a 0th-percentile earnings multiple.","kind":"consensus_expectation"},{"statement":"Consensus assigns close to zero option value to Agentforce/Data Cloud monetization at current multiples.","kind":"consensus_expectation"},{"statement":"Incremental ROIC of 4.9% implies recent M&A is earning below cost of capital, making buybacks the superior marginal use of capital at 20x earnings.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"FCF growing at roughly double the rate of revenue suggests underlying cash economics are improving despite the reported margin decline.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"The short-term setup (price below 20-day, negative MACD) favors accumulation on pullbacks toward the 50-day rather than chasing strength.","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"If agents monetize on top of the system of record rather than routing around it, CRM re-rates toward a materially higher multiple over the next 12-24 months.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"A further large debt-funded acquisition would convert this from a cash-return story into a value trap.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"Enterprise agent adoption will spend multiples of software cost on integration, data unification and trust/governance tooling, benefiting suppliers more reliably than the platform itself in the near term.","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"}],"confidence":0.58}},"technical":{"score":88,"passes":7,"criteria":{"above_150_200":true,"150_above_200":false,"200_rising_1m":true,"50_above_150_200":true,"above_50":true,"25pct_above_52w_low":true,"within_25pct_of_52w_high":true,"rs_positive_6m":true},"ready":true,"stage":"stage2_uptrend","close":238.22,"sma50":212.46,"sma150":190.42,"sma200":201.39,"sma150_prev4w":184.3,"sma150_declining":false,"pct_above_52w_low":58.7,"pct_from_52w_high":-10.5,"rs_6m":9.4,"rsi14":53.4,"atr20":11.105,"atr_pct":4.66,"overbought":false},"fundamentals":{"latest":{"period_end":"2026-07-31","filed":"2026-08-27","revenue":43938000000.0,"gross_profit":33956000000.0,"operating_income":8735000000.0,"net_income":9662000000.0,"ebitda":10226000000.0,"ocf":15750000000.0,"capex":596000000.0,"fcf":15154000000.0,"eps":10.96,"shares_diluted":896000000.0,"cash":11403000000.0,"debt":39288000000.0,"net_debt":27885000000.0,"equity":38378000000.0,"total_assets":109620000000.0,"rnd":6366000000.0,"sbc":3665000000.0,"buybacks":35070000000.0,"dividends":1515000000.0,"gross_margin":0.772816241066958,"operating_margin":0.1988028585734444,"net_margin":0.2199007692657836,"fcf_margin":0.34489507943010606,"fcf_conversion":1.5684123369902712,"revenue_growth":0.11229811148802593,"revenue_growth_prev":0.10981835142908958,"revenue_acceleration":0.0024797600589363533,"eps_growth":0.5930232558139534,"net_income_growth":0.45009755365451,"fcf_growth":0.2126110266463952,"operating_margin_change":-0.003389435487615805,"roic":0.11270361821046852,"incremental_roic":0.04904611031707477,"operating_income_estimated":false,"financial":false,"roe":0.2517588201573818,"roa":0.08814085020981573,"net_debt_to_ebitda":2.726872677488754,"interest_coverage":8.922369765066394,"dilution":-0.07390180878552977,"sbc_pct_revenue":0.08341299103281898,"tax_rate":0.221622492548135},"history":[{"period_end":"2022-10-31","filed":"2024-03-06","revenue":30294000000.0,"gr